      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_mLypsbaww3NmxWMqRChHex-bmuB2SBb5lTs6dzz2edjQ8=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "I'm listening from USA where our 2000 us lb short ton only makes 907.2 kilogram. 3000 tonnes over there( metric) would then be.....6,613,868 us pounds net( not counting the pallets/ dunnage weight( gross). Each skid can be approximately a 100 US pounds( 45 kilo). So just the net.....in US short tons( 2000 American pounds) is....3,307 American tons. Each single trailer truck over here carries from 22 to 25 US short tons depending on what type of trailer. Knocking off about 10% for metric tonnes( 1000 KG) leaves each single trailer on most US roads of 80000lb gross with metric equivalent of 19.958 to 22 680 metric per each single trailer load over here.",
      "likeCount": 1,
      "publishedAt": "2026-11-03T01:48:46Z",
