      "text": "An interesting overview… It’s a shame the place name pronunciations are so bad.  I travelled 16,000kms through much of this last year in a 30-year-old Land Rover Defender.  At that time Lake Eyre was full and Diamantina and Cooper were flowing, Simpson Desert (West of Birdsville) closed by floods.  But since then, the Oodnadatta track has been flooded, the Todd River in Alice has flowed twice and many other tracks through the centre closed by heavy rains.",
